    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## What the spec required\nThe `householdId` had to become **deterministic** \u2014 the first 12 hex chars of SHA\u2011256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` \u2014 so owners sharing last name and postcode automatically share it. `sharesHousehold` changes from *creating the link* to merely *bypassing the duplicate block*, and same\u2011(lastName, postcode) owners are now the same household: a second one is a 409 household duplicate unless it opts in, in which case it's a declared member and is **not** flagged as a possible duplicate.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Household identity (deterministic id)**\n- `Household.java` \u2014 rekeyed from (lastName, address) to (lastName, postcode); now exposes `normalizeLastName` and an `idFor(lastName, postcode)` returning the first 12 hex chars of the SHA\u2011256 (null when there's no postcode). Dropped the old address-based `matches`/`canonical`.\n- `AssignHousehold.java` \u2192 replaced by **`AssignHouseholdId.java`**, a single-responsibility step that just stamps the deterministic id onto the built owner. No more back-filling/linking of existing members.\n\n**Duplicate detection keyed off the computed id**\n- **`EnsureUniqueHousehold.java`** (new) \u2014 rejects a second owner whose `householdId` is already occupied with **409** via the new checked `HouseholdDuplicateException` (+ handler + escalation YAML, modeled on the existing 409 pairs), *unless* `sharesHousehold=true`, in which case it admits the owner and publishes a `DeclaredHouseholdMember` marker.\n- `DetectPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 now matches on `householdId` (the computed key) and **skips declared members** via that marker, implementing \"a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\"\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity` unchanged (still the exact-identity guard, meaningful for owners without a postcode); its and `CountHouseholdMembers`' javadoc updated. `CountHouseholdMembers` already sizes by `householdId`, so household size now flows from the deterministic id automatically.\n\n**Wiring & docs**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `assignHouseholdId` \u2192 `ensureUniqueHousehold` \u2192 `ensureUniqueIdentity`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 updated `sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions/examples to the new (lastName, postcode) semantics.\n\nTo keep responsibilities separated, the \"is this a declared member?\" decision lives solely in `EnsureUniqueHousehold` and is communicated to `DetectPossibleDuplicate` through a dedicated marker type (rather than a second `Boolean` variable, which would have collided with the existing `bulkSignupWarning` and forced `@Qualifier`s onto working code).\n\nBuild succeeds; `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
